<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">4 events that happened on 23 October, from 4004 BCE to 1983.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">4004 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Archbishop Ussher's date for the Creation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his chronology of 1650, Archbishop James Ussher calculated from biblical genealogies that the world was created on the evening before Sunday 23 October 4004 BCE. The date was printed in many English Bibles for two centuries.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1642</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royalists and Parliamentarians clash at Edgehill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles I's army fought Parliament's forces under the Earl of Essex at Edgehill in Warwickshire, the first pitched battle of the English Civil War. The indecisive result made clear the war would be long.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1956</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Hungarian Revolution begins in Budapest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A student demonstration in Budapest grew into a national uprising against the communist government and Soviet control. Soviet forces crushed it in November, leaving some 2,500 Hungarians dead and 200,000 in exile.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1983</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Truck bombs kill 241 US and 58 French troops in Beirut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Suicide bombers drove explosive-laden trucks into the US Marine barracks and a French paratroop building in Beirut. The attacks led to the withdrawal of the multinational peacekeeping force from Lebanon.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a></div></li></ol>
